      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>"Offices of the 'Cycle Trader' and the DRAR SIRS, 'Motor Trader; 15th Vov., 1907. " I have driven the car for over 55,700 miles, and have never been 'hung up ' through mechanical troubles. In this mileage is included a Scottish tour, a couple of tours in Devonshire, And one in Wales, be- sides regular use between London and the Midlands. I may say the car has given me every satisfaction. This, I think, is all the more remark- able as it is the first year I have driven a car, and further, that after the first three months I have been without the assistance of a mechanician. "Yours faithfully, (Signed) "J. MACKENZIE. PRICES FROM FREE TRIALS £235. ARRANGED. Complete Specifications on applications to : BELtIAN tk. DAVIES, SANKEY STREET,</p>
      </div>
