        <p>Mrs. W. B Roberts's Concert. We are pleased to state that as a result of the recent concert organized by Mrs. NV. B. Roberts, and at which her orchestra and several well known artistes appeared, the handsome sum of £22 lis. sd. has been handed over to the Infirmary extension fund. Finest DANISH BuTTErt, Is. 2d. lb. at ASHLEY'S.—Advt. Personal. At the annual conference in connection with the Lancashire Congregational Union held at Bolton this week, the Rev. John Yonge was appointed one of the delegates to the International Congregatiomal Council to be held at Edinburgh from June 30th to July 10th. Off-Licence Holders. At the monthly meeting of the Warrington Off-Licence Holders' Protection Association, Mr. Throssell (president) and Mr. Robert Smith (secretary) were appointed delegates to the annual conference of the National Federation to be held at Grimsby on April Ist. Mr. Throssell was also nominated for the Ewcutive Committee of the Federation.</p>
        <p>Premier in game, Premier in quality. PREMIER CYCLES from 6 guineas.—J. S. GARLAND, 51 to 55 Bridge-street, Warrington.—Advt. Education Committee. The monthly meeting of the Education Committee will be held at the Town Hall on Monday evening at , six o'clock. The School Management Committee has instructed the Director to communicate again with the Town Hall, Parks and Baths Committhe with a view, if possible' to some arrangement being made by which school girls may have the benefit of the existing bathing accommodation at the batks on say two days each week during the approaching season. For Bronchial Coughs take Woods' Great Peppermint Cure. 1/11, 219.—Advt. Church Society Addresses. A. special service for women arranged by the Church Society was held in the Parish Church yesterday afternoon and was very largely attended. The Rev. Canon Kempthorne, Rector of Liverpool, delivered an impressive address. In the evening the weekly service for men was held when Canon lamp- thorn° addressed a large gathering on " Facing the Facts." Next Friday evening the Rev. Peter Green, of Manchester, will give an address On " Christ and Him Crucified." MOUNTAIN FLAX (LiNum CAMIARTICIIM) PILLS An agreeable aperient. Worth a trial. 91d.—Advt. Local Artistes at Earlestown. A highly successful concert organized by the Brunswick Male Voice Choir was held at the Earles- town Town Hall on Thursday evening. The choir gave selections in excellent style and the other artistes were Miss Olive Clare, 11A.M. (soprano), Miss Lily Fairhurst (contralto), Mr. P. J. George (baritone), Lyric Prize Quartet, and Master Tom Barton (violin). Mr. W. H. Payton, Mus, Bac. was the accompanist. A most interesting programme was submitted and encores were freely accorded.</p>
