      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0176" n="art0176">
        <head>BUTCHER BIRD'S FREE LUNCH.</head>
        <p>THE BUTCHER BIRD'S FREE LUNCH.</p>
        <p>When the 'barbed, wire fence first came into use in California cattle owners blamed the in- ventor. Not so the butcher bird. The butcher bird, is a creature about the size of a small crow, and he lives on insects and smaller birds. When the butcher bird saw the first barbed wite fence he lighted upon it, flapped his wings three times, and crowed. He had discovered what he had wanted for a long .time. At first the farmers who instituted the barbed. wire wondered how so many grasshoppers, beetles, fieldmice, and small birds became im- paled upon the barbs of their fence wires. They soon. learned, for the butcher bird is not a. secretive creature. When grasshoppers and, other insects, were plentiful he gathered great stores and stuck them on the barbs of the fences. When.ltard times came, the barbed wire fence was to him like a free lunch counter. Now, in winter time if, is no rare thing in parts. of California to see the butcher bird hopping along the fence wires continually picking his meals as he skips from barb to barb. _</p>
        <p>GERTRUDE M. CLARKE.</p>
        <p>Dear Uncle Ned,—l am very much interested in reading the tales and pieces of poetry in the Children's Corner. I have a. friend who is a member, and now I wish very much to become one of your many nieces.—l remain your loving niece, EMMA INMAN.</p>
        <p>Neighbour's Boy (looking through the fence): "My father's a heap bigger man than yourn I" New Boy: "Sire ain't nothin' When my father coughs, you can hear him half a mile I''</p>
        <p>"One might have heard a pin fall," is a expression of silence; but it has been eclipsed by the French phrase. "You might have heard the unfolding of a lady's pocket handkerchief."'</p>
        <p>What's that in the fire and not in the flame? What's that in the master and not in the dame?' What's that in the courtier and not the clown?. What's that in the country sad not in th town?</p>
