      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>LUMBAGO IN. HIS LOINS. A HARD WOIIKEII CRIPPLED. His Painful Disorder Cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</head>
        <p>LUMBAGO IN. HIS LOINS. A HARD WOIIKEII CRIPPLED. His Painful Disorder Cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>Few men, whatever their station in life may he, escape altogether from Lumbago, or Muscular Rheumatism. It is a treacherous enemy that often attacks the most active man and prostrates him without warning. Mr. John Smith, who resides at 16, Hanover-street, Oldham, and has been a lifelong toiler in a busy Lancashire foundry, was a victim of Acute Lumbago until Dr. Williams' Pink Pills cured him.</p>
        <p>To a reporter he gave the following account : " For many years," said Mr. Smith "I was a martyr to sudden attacks of Lumbago in my loins, and the repeated attacks of this painful malady left me so weak that work was all but impossible. "Yes, I have to work hard, and it has been a common occurrence for me to leave my place of employment hot and tired, yet after a few minuos in the open air I would tremble violently with chilliness.</p>
        <p>"One day I felt as cold as though my blood had frozen, and later my temperature went up to fever heat. From. that day I did not know what health was.</p>
        <p>"At night my rest was "I was bending down when broken, for every move- a sharp pain .flew meat excited excruciat- through my loins." ing torture through nerves and muscles. I ached In all ray bones, and fel utterly worn out.</p>
        <p>TIIE CLIMAX CAXIE when one day, as I was bending down, a sharp pain flew through my loins and it seemed as though the muscles of my back had broken. " The whole of my back felt scourged : and after I had been assisted into a reclining position I could scarcely rise again. I poulticed my back and then tried the common remedies for Rheumatism and Lumbago but these only aggravated my sufferings. "My blood was watery and my flesh had wasted away. I became irritable and unreasonable through the continual pain, and was quite unfit for work. Instead of eating heartily I did little more than taste a meal and then put it aside.</p>
