        <p>Sores at Scabs A Zam-Buk cure at Nelson. To the long list of parents who o we Zam-Buk a debt of sincere gratitude must now be added Mr.and Mrs. Postron of 13,Thomas-street,Nelson, Lancashire, whose little seven-year-old son was ;10',;ifr,L ',1112.5t perfectly cured by this unique balm of a trouble- some bad leg caused by a kick. ("N " One day " said Mrs. Rostron to a' Leader " representative, " he came home suffer- _ ing from a nasty kick on the leg, received while playing football. I bandaged the wound as well 7 . as I could, but instead of improving it gradually §P/h got worse, and the sores and scabs which had formed increased in length. Being alarmed we went to a chemist and got some medicine, and also tried all manner of salves recommended by neighbours. It was all in vain, however, and '.• all the expense brought no improvement. , " When I was coming home one night a A. neighbour asked me how the boy was getting : • • on, and, when I said he was no better, she MASTER ROSTRON. recommended me to try Zam-Buk, as she knew it had effected a cure in a case in which she was interested. When I got home I sent for some Zam-Buk and used a large quantity on one bandage, which I kept on for two days. "I saw the leg looked better so I thought I would give Zam-Buk a fair trial. I got a 2s. 9d. box and the boy's leg improved wonderfully. The balm had a very soothing effect, and soon the discharges, which had been very frequent, ceased altox,ether, and new skin was formed. The boy is qnite right again now and I attribute his cure solely to Zam-Buk. My husband and I were getting quite 'down in the dumps ' about the way the wound was spreading, but thanks to Zam-Buk our boy is now quite himself again. "I can now, thorrMghly recommend Zam-Buk for it cured where all other remedies failed."</p>
