        <p>CHILD'S PURCHASE OF WHISKY. At St. Helens County Petty Sessions, on Tuesday, William Thomas Ball, landlord of the Star Inn, Rain- ford, was charged with serving whisky to a girl under fourteen, and James Harrison, a District Council mad- man, was charged with sending his niece, Minnie Harrison, for the whisky. The girl's age was given as twelve years.—%lr. E. NV. Swift, who defended, con- tended that the onus of proving that the defendant knew that the child was under fourteen lay on the prosecution.—The Chairman said the Bench found Ball guilty because be wilfully took no steps to ascertain the age of the child, and was thereby criminally negli- gent, not caring whether she was under or over fourteen ; he would be tined 20s. and costs. Harrison was fined 2s. 6d. and costs.</p>
